WEBVTT

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:49.010
The lockdown is for 24 hours.

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:49.800
Understood?

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:50.970
Yes, sir.

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:55.260
Take this.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:58.390
Personal effects are prohibited.

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:00.230
Are you sure about that?

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:02.520
The rules are complicated.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.900
I don't have them all memorized.

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:13.570
Lt. Soma.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:16.410
Tell me.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.540
What are you thinking?

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:27.380
You remind me of the song of Oberon.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:32.050
"Never mole, hare-lip,
nor scar, nor mark prodigious..."

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.180
A Midsummer Night's Dream, huh?

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:37.470
Appropriate to the season, no?

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:42.850
But the seasons do change so quickly.

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:45.230
Was it only as recent as spring...

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:50.490
...when your heart was broken
by one who didn't fancy you?

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:55.070
Oh, sorry for upsetting you.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:59.160
But you've known of the lessons
of Faust and Mephisto.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:03.250
There are consequences
when you barter with the devil.

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:07.500
You can't claim that
you've never been warned.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.260
What are we talking about?

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:11.760
Our hero of the day, Frank.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:15.390
You...

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.770
Ryu Soma?

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.110
So that's why...

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:30.360
...I'm reminding you today not to be
upset by how things work out.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.610
I haven't forgotten our agreement.

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:38.700
The second batch of goods, eh?

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.620
Very nice.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.120
I await the next one.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:46.670
Pictures of Funeral's beautiful SARGs.

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:48.590
Lt. Soma!

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:51.420
It's time to go back.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:03:58.770
Forgive me.

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:00.100
This man is my...

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.060
Man?

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:04.310
No.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.440
Never mind.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:11.070
Why is it you always act suspicious?

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:13.410
I was just...

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:16.530
...enjoying the evening breeze.

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:30.050
Give and take.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:32.010
The basis of relationships.

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:34.640
Especially between men and women.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:38.600
You give and take something
by remaining Ryu Soma.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:43.270
The SARGs are aeronautically
engineered, state-of-the-art,

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:45.360
and replicate the human form.

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:14.550
Furthermore,

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:16.350
What functions as a plane

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:20.350
can utilize the power
of martial arts on the ground.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:49.920
But the point to remember
is that the on-ground power

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:51.880
isn't lost in the air.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:54.390
I'm attaching detailed data.

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:57.810
They are designed to
look like planes in the air.

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:12.740
The reason, if one thinks about it,

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:16.650
is so that ordinary citizens...

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:22.250
...do not mistake them for aliens.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:36.260
However, this choice is in part
due to the SARG's "A Motor";

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:40.020
In other words,
a human copy of an alien motor.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:46.900
Even Funeral's engineers
don't understand how they work.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:51.530
Maintenance of the SARGs
is handled through the military.

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:00.620
As a security procedure?

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:06.090
But there haven't been
any national wars in ages.

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:07.170
Of course...

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:12.630
Of course, there are
always humans like me.

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:19.890
As detailed as possible.

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:21.890
As simple as you can.

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:25.440
Easy, like writing in a diary.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.110
A little love diary between us.

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:32.280
Right? Is this fine?

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:42.000
The EX-1 destroyed
a Type H2 in the yellow zone.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:57.390
The newly classified M-1 was stopped
before it entered the red zone.

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:23.120
Three divisions were set after
the first "Close Encounter War."

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:27.500
The yellow zone, the red zone,
and the dark zone.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:30.950
The concentric circles
are labeled by hazard...

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:36.140
...and surround the place all
the aliens seem to be drawn to.

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:43.190
A place known as the Pilgrimage Point.

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:44.520
The place where...

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:58.290
I heard you were a pilot in Alaska
before you came here.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:01.620
What was that like?

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:03.120
Nothing special.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:05.750
It was a living.

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:17.390
Nothing wrong with that.

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:22.560
The captain and I used to
be in dangerous operations.

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:27.110
Lt. Soma?

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:29.070
Hmph.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:40.870
Excuse me.

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:45.210
Here's the report on conditions at HQ.

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:47.290
Thank you.

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:56.050
Is that the EX-1's dossier?

00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:59.560
The tapestry of aliens.

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:02.560
That's what Lt. Simmons
and the others called him.

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:04.440
If you think of it,

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:10.990
scrap is inferior to the original,
but a tapestry can be more.

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:15.950
Cats and dogs are stronger
than pure breeds when mixed.

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:18.580
The same may hold true for mixing species.

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:27.550
I leave the lieutenants to you...

00:10:27.550 --> 00:10:31.130
...but I have my doubts
whether it's for the best.

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:33.550
When I was in the army...

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:36.350
...I had two men who hated each other.

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:38.770
So you locked them up, too?

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:41.850
No, I put them on the same plane.

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:44.230
As the pilot and gunner.

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:47.610
They fought aliens,
bickering the whole time.

00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:51.490
But the two were the force's best team.

00:10:51.490 --> 00:10:52.820
Men are lucky.

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:54.360
Male bonding.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:56.780
But that team is no more...

00:10:58.830 --> 00:11:03.580
Men back each other up quickly
when there's a common purpose.

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:06.380
Will we be the same way?

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:12.340
I've always backed you up.

00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:14.510
In the past, in the present...

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:16.640
and I'll continue to do so.

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:17.680
I see.

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:19.350
Carry on then.

00:11:19.350 --> 00:11:20.350
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:26.020 --> 00:11:27.980
A common purpose...

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:51.880
Big Brother, how are things?

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:54.370
Is it hot where you are?

00:11:54.370 --> 00:11:59.380
I've been playing lacrosse every day
since we have a match soon.

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:02.890
Look how much sun I'm getting.

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:07.320
Anyway, Big Brother...

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:14.660
Could you send Father
some mail once in a while?

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:18.290
I know things were tense
when you left home.

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:20.200
But...

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:27.550
Why don't you write a reply?

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:31.260
Tell her how her darling brother
is in lockdown.

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:42.270
Room service. Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:12:42.270 --> 00:12:43.520
Where's the guard?

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:45.400
We're short-handed.

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:48.320
We all have to pitch in.

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:51.900
That's why yours truly signed on so quickly.

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:53.950
I've tried to help.

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:55.740
And not get in the way.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:01.210
Your neighbor doesn't seem too happy.

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:11.550
You know what happened to
SARG 2's sub-pilot, don't you?

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:14.090
I read about it.

00:13:14.090 --> 00:13:15.510
I'm glad you did.

00:13:15.510 --> 00:13:18.720
His colleagues couldn't even eat for a time.

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:25.020
This may not be a real war,
but these are war-like conditions.

00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:30.490
Don't forget that the only ones
you can trust are in your unit.

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:37.030
Here's something I'll share
so you can pass the time.

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:19.450
It's too big for me.

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:21.160
Don't be so picky.

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:23.500
It'll get bigger.

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:24.460
What?

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:26.750
It's going to get even bigger?

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:28.710
Your body will!

00:14:30.460 --> 00:14:32.590
Okay, I can take it in a bit.

00:14:39.470 --> 00:14:42.230
The G-force suits are just for protection.

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:44.690
This is fine for now.

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:47.690
How are the two in lockup?

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:49.940
This is letting them rest.

00:14:49.940 --> 00:14:52.700
Want to join them, Sue?

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:55.410
Sir, no thank you, sir!

00:14:57.490 --> 00:15:01.620
I dunno about Dan, but it'll be
good medicine for the other guy.

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:10.570
W-What is it, Sue?

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:13.840
A 20th century jacket's so cool.

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:15.340
Lend it to me.

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:16.800
No, it's mine!

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:17.890
Just a bit!

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:18.890
<i>No!
Come on, Please?</i>

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:18.900
Come on, Please?

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:19.270
<i>You can't!</i>

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:20.520
Hattie, wait!

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:22.850
A relic from the most elite team...

00:15:22.850 --> 00:15:25.360
...and it's just an antique to her.

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:31.570
Father?

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:46.960
Father, I...

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:26.960
Never mind.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:37.180
Are you really going?

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.970
Eavesdropping, were you?

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:41.100
Bad girl.

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:45.730
Don't change the subject!

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:49.320
You're going to go fight, aren't you?

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:50.440
Father is...

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.160
...one of life's losers.

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:55.530
How could you...

00:16:55.530 --> 00:17:00.660
All he ever does since Mother died
is build those models.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:08.130
She was the last one to disagree
with him and she killed herself.

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:11.380
I don't want that.

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:16.010
I don't want to be a millionaire's son
who sits and counts bodies.

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:18.550
So I'm going to the front lines.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:20.180
But...

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:24.020
If I lose my brother, too...

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:24.980
I...

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:34.200
I promise you.

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:36.200
You'll never lose me.

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:37.480
I won't die.

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:39.240
Really?

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:41.620
So you promise me.

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:43.210
Don't cry anymore.

00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:48.460
And wherever I am,
I want you to send me a smile.

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:51.760
I'll send you mail.

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:53.760
Lots.

00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:58.930
You're a good girl.

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:11.820
Elaine?

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:13.780
Can't be...

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:46.020
What is it?

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:48.530
Nothing.

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:50.320
I have nothing to report.

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:51.280
Bastard.

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:53.410
You're always like that.

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:55.280
Too bad I can't hit you.

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:56.990
You can anytime.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.580
Don't make me laugh!

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:00.830
I don't ever want to be back here!

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:09.170
I won't do anything like that again.

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:38.830
Level S?

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.500
Pretty highly classified.

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:49.210
Don't bother.

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:52.010
We're not authorized
for those kinds of searches.

00:19:52.010 --> 00:19:53.890
What a coincidence.

00:19:54.930 --> 00:19:57.310
This is the second time we've met here.

00:19:58.430 --> 00:20:01.100
I'm here to satisfy my curiosity.

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:03.350
What's your excuse, Lieutenant?

00:20:04.940 --> 00:20:06.650
If you'll excuse me.

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:07.610
Hold on!

00:20:09.150 --> 00:20:10.780
You're always like this.

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:13.450
Moving around the place like a ghost!

00:20:13.450 --> 00:20:16.530
Now that you mention it you could be right.

00:20:16.530 --> 00:20:20.600
Maybe Ryu Soma is just a ghost
from another time.

00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:22.160
Stop playing around!

00:20:25.960 --> 00:20:28.500
Sounding the alarm could be a problem.

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:29.630
Bastard...

00:20:34.640 --> 00:20:36.100
Are you finished?

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:37.350
What?

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:38.970
Keep going.

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:41.680
I doubt my face could get any worse.

00:20:47.710 --> 00:20:49.860
Fine, you asked for it!

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:52.450
Lieutenant, please stop!

00:20:52.450 --> 00:20:53.990
Lt. Simmons!

00:20:53.990 --> 00:20:54.990
Lieutenant!

00:20:54.990 --> 00:20:56.910
Let me go!

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:06.000
Emergency code 1302.

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:07.500
Defense level yellow.

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:09.260
Alien sighting confirmed.

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:11.630
Request Funeral assistance.

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:13.680
Send someone to Floor 11.

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:18.180
Lt. Soma and Lt. Simmons
are to be released at once...

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:20.270
...and to report for regular duty.

00:21:21.310 --> 00:21:23.560
I assume that's okay,
Commander?

00:21:23.810 --> 00:21:25.230
Of course.

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:26.520
However...

00:21:28.190 --> 00:21:30.860
Will they be able to fight together?

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:33.740
Even soldiers with personal differences...

00:21:33.740 --> 00:21:37.870
...can back each other up
in combat when they have to.

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:41.830
So you've said.

00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:51.050
Listen, no matter who we face,
we're on the same team.

00:21:51.050 --> 00:21:53.800
No more insubordination.

00:21:53.800 --> 00:21:54.780
Got it?

00:21:54.780 --> 00:21:59.420
I do what I can to respect authority
and follow the rules.

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:01.810
You never change, do you?

00:22:01.810 --> 00:22:06.190
I don't know if I'll ever
be able to understand you.

00:22:08.400 --> 00:22:11.360
You may always be like an alien to me.

00:22:12.360 --> 00:22:13.280
Whatever.

00:22:13.700 --> 00:22:15.530
Let's go, Lieutenant!

00:22:15.570 --> 00:22:16.450
Yes, sir!

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:35.010
Memories and Loneliness

00:22:36.260 --> 00:22:39.060
No dreams of cradles that rock.

00:22:40.100 --> 00:22:41.810
Alone in this tower.

00:22:42.690 --> 00:22:45.440
I can only move myself.

00:22:46.400 --> 00:22:49.150
Next time,
Loneliness and Sorrow.
